[3.6704, "o", "\r\n"]
[3.8904, "o", "  seals that claim no generation   31  of 1428\r\n  distinct specs behind them       16\r\n\r\n  A hollow seal passes every SEAL check. spec_hash matches the file,\r\n  so `seals fresh` is green. `none` equals `none`, so `seals drift`\r\n  reports zero. The file exists, so Seal Coverage counts the spec as\r\n  covered. The one thing it does not record is the output.\r\n\r\n  Most of these are already written down as debt elsewhere -- the\r\n  reconciliation below says how many. The seal side is where the same\r\n  fact reads as health.\r\n"]
[3.8905, "o", "\r\n  against tools/specs_generate_baseline.txt, which calls each line a debt\r\n        13  already recorded there\r\n         3  hollow seal, NOT in the ledger\r\n"]
[3.8905, "o", "         1  in the ledger with no hollow seal\r\n\r\n  sealed, but not a spec  3\r\n"]
[3.8905, "o", "      docs/nona-03-manifest/PHI_LOOP_CONTRACT.md\r\n      docs/nona-03-manifest/SOUL.md\r\n      specs/sandbox/sandbox.tri\r\n\r\n  where they are\r\n         4  specs/physics\r\n"]
[3.8905, "o", "         2  docs/nona-03-manifest\r\n         2  specs/ar\r\n         2  specs/benchmarks\r\n         2  specs/test_framework\r\n         1  examples/fpga\r\n         1  specs/api\r\n         1  specs/conformance\r\n         1  specs/sandbox\r\n\r\n  --why runs the compiler on each and groups the errors: it turns\r\n  16 specs into the handful of parser gaps behind them.\r\n"]
